    "caveats": "Non-significant difference is not evidence of equivalence; CI includes both negative and positive values."
   },
   {
    "finding_id": "F2",
    "summary": "Skua achieved a significantly higher held-out success rate than Plover-PG (secondary endpoint): mean 44.63% vs 40.50%, paired t-test t=4.05, p=0.0029, 95% CI [1.82, 6.44] percentage points for the mean paired difference.",
