   "passage": "On the 200 held-out Mirefield levels, Skua did not significantly differ from Plover-PG in mean normalized return (primary endpoint; 62.95 ± 5.04 vs 62.04 ± 4.29; paired t-test t=1.18, p=0.27, 95% CI [-0.84, 2.66]). However, Skua achieved a significantly higher held-out success rate (secondary endpoint; 44.63% ± 3.85 vs 40.50% ± 4.78; paired t-test t=4.05, p=0.0029, 95% CI [1.82, 6.44] percentage points). Thus, the results are mixed: Skua improved the secondary success-rate metric but not the primary normalized-return metric relative to Plover-PG.",
